  "question": {
    "text": "In an atom, the total number of electrons having quantum numbers <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>|</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> and <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0,1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2,3</mn></math><br /><math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></math><br />For <math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#160;</mi></math><br />So, six electrons can have <math><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">l</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> &amp; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> .<br />&nbsp;",
